From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 the blocked list's page is the primary main frame's, and says when it is an error page

tab/098 named the tab's own site in ReArcTabCopyBlockedHosts' reply ("page")
from WebContents::GetLastCommittedURL(), and said in its header and in
C-ABI.md "the primary main frame's committed address". tab/096 has a helper
for a tab's site, SiteOf, which reads the primary main frame's committed
origin. The consistency review of the range asked for one of the two, or
words that match the code (REVIEW-efda98e4-1777874b.md, 10; it bears on
security BL-10 and BL-11).

What Chromium does, read at the pin:

- WebContentsImpl::GetLastCommittedURL() is the last committed navigation
  entry's virtual URL: the address bar's text. It is not a frame's URL, and
  for an entry with a virtual URL the two differ.
- RenderFrameHost::GetLastCommittedURL() is the frame's. On an error page it
  "continues to return the failed destination target URL", and Chromium's
  header says of both functions that they "should not be used directly for
  security, authorization, or permission checks without verifying
  !IsErrorDocument()".
- RenderFrameHost::GetLastCommittedOrigin(), which tab/096 reads, is opaque
  on an error page, so tab/096 answers "no site" there.

So this reply now reads the primary main frame, as tab/096 does, and its
committed URL, not the entry's. It does not take the origin, as tab/096
does: a page whose own request the blocker stopped is an error page, and
that is the one page where "Turn Off Blocking for This Site" is the way in.
With the origin it would have no site and the switch would refuse. The
reply says instead when the frame is an error document ("error": true), and
the host writes no rule between two sites from such a page (Allow), because
no document of that site is loaded. The switch for the site alone stays.

No new call and no change to the header but the comment: a host tells a
reply of this bridge from one of 0.79.0 by the key. Nothing else of the
reply changes.

Type-checked with the tree's clang from a scratch view, then built on
2026-11-20 in out/ReArc-codecs-arm64 (overlay 6274321b22): the framework
carries bridge 0.80.0 and still exports both calls of tab/098; the series
replays 117 of 117 to the pin's tree and to the head's.
engine/tests/check_blocked_hosts_patch.py holds the frame, the flag, and
that the navigation entry is no longer read. Not run: no page has been
loaded on this engine, and no self-test step makes an error page.

Touches: chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/{rearc_content_blocker.cc,
rearc_engine_abi.h, rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm}.
Applies after tab/098 (the same lines of the bridge file and the header).

Bridge 0.80.0, ABI 1.69 unchanged, no new feature string. No struct changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-20 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.109 (overlay 9f2767b4c1).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc
index 4a39321..49dc9fd 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_content_blocker.cc
@@ -88,6 +88,7 @@
 #include "content/public/browser/navigation_handle.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/navigation_throttle.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/navigation_throttle_registry.h"
+#include "content/public/browser/render_frame_host.h"
 #include "content/public/browser/web_contents.h"
 #include "extensions/browser/api/declarative_net_request/action_tracker.h"
 #include "extensions/browser/api/declarative_net_request/composite_matcher.h"
@@ -1204,7 +1205,8 @@ std::optional<std::string> BlockedListId(const extensions::Extension& blocker,
 // up, as the counts are. The sites are never logged.
 // "page" is the tab's own site, from the same function and so the same
 // public suffix list as the blocked sites: the site of the primary main
-// frame's committed address, http and https only. The host writes "allow this
+// frame's committed address, http and https only, with "error" for an error
+// document (tab/099). The host writes "allow this
 // host on this site" from the two names of one reply, and reads the reply
 // again before it writes: an address that is only pending is not in it
 // (security BL-10, BL-11).
@@ -1272,14 +1274,29 @@ std::string BlockedHostsJson(uint64_t tab_id) {
   }
   base::DictValue reply;
   if (contents) {
-    const GURL& page = contents->GetLastCommittedURL();
+    // The page is the primary main frame's document, the frame tab/096 reads
+    // a site's permissions from (SiteOf, its committed origin). tab/098 read
+    // the navigation entry's virtual URL here (WebContents::
+    // GetLastCommittedURL), which is the address bar's text and not a
+    // frame's: for a page with a virtual URL the two differ. This reads the
+    // frame's committed URL. It cannot use the origin as tab/096 does: on an
+    // error page the origin is opaque and there would be no site, and a page
+    // whose own request the blocker stopped is an error page, the one place
+    // where turning blocking off for that site is the way in. On an error
+    // document the committed URL is the address that failed (Chromium:
+    // "should not be used directly for security, authorization, or permission
+    // checks without verifying !IsErrorDocument()"), so the reply says so
+    // ("error") and the host writes no rule between two sites from it.
+    content::RenderFrameHost* frame = contents->GetPrimaryMainFrame();
+    const GURL& page = frame->GetLastCommittedURL();
     std::string page_site;
     bool page_is_one_site = false;
     if (page.SchemeIsHTTPOrHTTPS() &&
         dnr::ActionTracker::GetSiteOfUrl(page, &page_site, &page_is_one_site)) {
       reply.Set("page", base::DictValue()
                             .Set("host", std::move(page_site))
-                            .Set("registrable", page_is_one_site));
+                            .Set("registrable", page_is_one_site)
+                            .Set("error", frame->IsErrorDocument()));
     }
   }
   reply.Set("hosts", std::move(hosts));
diff --git a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_abi.h b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_abi.h
index 2df52cb..152031d 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_abi.h
+++ b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_abi.h
@@ -1926,14 +1926,19 @@ REARC_ENGINE_EXPORT ReArcStatus ReArcWebAuthnRespond(uint64_t request_id,
 // Blocked hosts (content_blocking_hosts, ABI 1.69): what ReArcTabGetBlockedCount
 // counts, by site, for a "Blocked on this page" list. *json is +1 malloc,
 // NUL-terminated UTF-8; free with ReArcBufferFree.
-//   {"page":{"host":"example.com","registrable":true},
+//   {"page":{"host":"example.com","registrable":true,"error":false},
 //    "hosts":[{"host":"doubleclick.net","count":3,"registrable":true,
 //              "lists":["easylist"]}],"more":0}
 // page: the tab's own site, named as a blocked one is, from the primary main
 // frame's committed address; absent when that is not http or https. A host
 // that writes a rule "allow this host on this site" takes both names from one
 // reply, and reads the reply again before it writes: if page has changed, the
-// tab has moved on and nothing is written.
+// tab has moved on and nothing is written. error (bridge 0.80.0): the frame
+// shows an error page, and host is the site of the address that failed, not
+// of a document of that site. A host writes no such rule from it; a setting
+// for that site alone (blocking off for it) is still the person's to make. A
+// reply without the key is from bridge 0.79.0, which took the address from
+// the navigation entry and did not say.
 // host: the registrable domain of a blocked request's host (private
 // registries count: "someone.github.io"), lower-case ASCII (punycode); the
 // host itself when it has no registrable domain. registrable: the name is
diff --git a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm
index 52f630e..d26be2a 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm
+++ b/chrome/browser/rearc_bridge/rearc_engine_entry_mac.mm
@@ -45,7 +45,7 @@ bool HandleTerminateCancel() override {
 
 const char* ReArcEngineBridgeVersion(void) {
   CHECK([NSThread isMainThread]);
-  return "0.79.0";
+  return "0.80.0";
 }
 
